					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MAGNITUDE\n\nThe Magnitude node computes the magnitude of a value.\n\nIn vector math, magnitude is all about the length of the vector. \nImagine an arrow pointing in some direction. \nThat arrow is your vector. \nThe magnitude tells you how long that arrow actually is.\n\nThis is however, different than the Distance node.\nThe magnitude is calculated from 0 to the vector.\nThe Distance node calculates the distances between two vectors."
					}
				},
