			"68": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: COLOR FROM CENTER\n\nIn this example we place Circle shapes in a Grid pattern.\nNext we assign color to two shapes based their Magnitude.\n\nThe Grid Pattern provides us with a collection of Float 2's - our vectors.\nNext we calculate the Magnitude of each vector, this gives us their length and thus how \"far\" they are away from the center.\nWe normalize the magnitude by dividing it by the highest value in the collection (using the Max node).\nThis is done because the Crossfader node wants a normalized 0-1 input range.\n\nAs a result we are crossfading between Red and Blue depending on the magnitude of the position of the circle."
					}
				},
